JSON-RPC: video settings and chapters of the current playback; Player.Open file check.

Player.GetVideoSettings and Player.SetVideoSettings read and change the per-video settings of the
current playback like the video and audio settings dialogs do (picture, view mode, deinterlacing,
scaling, tone mapping, volume amplification, center mix level), and report the renderer features
and the deinterlacing and scaling methods available for the current video. Player.GetChapters
lists the chapters of the current playback (index as used by Kodi, title, start in seconds).

Player.Open (and every method taking an item with a "file") checked that a local file exists
through the directory cache: once Kodi had listed a folder, for example to look for external
subtitles, a file created in it later was reported missing and the method failed with "Invalid
params". The check now bypasses the cache.

